title: Last Push
new-page: true
view-if: electoral_rally_timer >= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; electoral_rally_timer += 12
max-visits: 36
is-card: true
card-image: img/electioncampaign.jpg
frequency: 100
tags: - #election_campaign

= Last Push

Our election machine is humming along. But the costs are running high.

We may have enough resources for one last large scale campaign this election: What issues should headline its flyers?

- @workers: "The Housing Crisis: A Socialist Solution."
- @homeowners: "Dont let the Banks rip you off! Strengthen the State Mortgages."
- @public: "The Welfare State: [+ year + 10 +]."
- @private: [? if a_in_government != 1 : "This Bourgious Government? A Costly Affair." ?][? if a_in_government = 1 : "Highlight the economic achievements of our government." ?]
- @rural: Target the rural population with a revived: "Denmark for the people!" campaign
- @unemployed: "Work for all!"
- @youth: Let us target the youth: [? if vietnam_relations >= 1 : "Democratize the Universities!" ?] [? if vietnam_relations = 2 and year <= 1976 : "Peace in Vietnam!" ?]
- @small_campaign2: Since we can't afford anything big, let us reprint various earlier flyers.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@workers
subtitle: -2 resources – This will satisfy Working class tenants, our traditional base.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: -2 resources – Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; prole_a += 8*(1-globalization)*efc; public_prole_a += 7*efc; memberrise += 1.2*efc; homeowner_a -= 2/efc; public_homeowner_a -= 2/efc;

By focussing the campaign on traditional socialist issues, while expanding our work in the tenant movements, we have increased our campaigning among the proletarians. [? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract workers. ?]

@public
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; public_prole_a += 4*efc; public_homeowner_a += 3*efc; memberrise += 1*efc; homeowner_a -= 2*efc; rural_a += 1*efc; prole_a += 2*efc

Public sector workers, have felt neglected by us in the past.

By focussing the campaign on strenghtening the welfare state, we have bettered our standing among them. The poorer [? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract workers. ?]

@private
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; prole_a += 6*(1-globalization)*efc; homeowner += 3*efc*(1-globalization); memberrise += 0.3*efc*(1-globalization)

Private sector workers, the backbone of the workers movement.

By focussing our campaign on the labour struggle, we have increased our campaigning among the workers of the private sector.

@homeowners
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; homeowner_a += 10*(1-globalization)*efc; public_homeowner_a += 10*efc; rural_a += 8*efc; pettyb_a += 5*efc; memberrise += 1.4*efc*(1-globalization); sf_relation -= 6; dkp_relation -= 4; vs_relation -= 6

The "new middle class" of homeowning workers.

By doubling down on the protection of state mortgages and stable socialist leadership, we have increased our standing among the new middle class – the workers who own their homes. In fact homeowners in general see us in a more positive light. [? if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0: The popular antipathy towards socialism among this group makes our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?] [? if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0: The high levels of nationalism among this group make our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?]

@rural
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; rural_a += 5*(1-globalization); rural_spd -= 3*efc if peoples_party == 0; resources -= 2; peoples_party_support += 1; rural_spd += 3*efc if rural_policy >= 2

By promising protectionist measures against banks and multinationals, we have increased our campaigning among the small businessowners in the city as well as countryside. [? if peoples_party == 0: We have not historically campaigned much among the farmers, and they do not trust us. ?][? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among farmers than before. ?][? if rural_policy >= 2 : Our rural policies have made it easier for us to build support among farmers. ?]

@unemployed
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; unemployed_a += 6*(1-globalization); resources -= 2; unemployed_a -= 3 if welfare < 0; unemployed_a += 6*efc if wtb_adopted = 1; memberrise += 0.2*efc*(1-globalization); unemployed_a += 3*efc if welfare >= 2;

By promising public works programs and stable socialist leadership, we have increased our campaigning among the unemployed. [? if welfare < 0: The welfare cuts and resultant poverty make our campaign more difficult, since we are associated with the government that enacted these cuts, and our campaign may even backfire. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract support from the unemployed. ?]

@youth
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; unemployed_a += 5*(1.1-globalization)*efc; prole_a += 2*efc; public_prole_a += 1*efc; rural_a +=2*efc

By focussing on our comitment to international social justice, we have increased our campaigning among the youth.


@small_campaign2
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; unemployed_a += 1*(1.1-globalization)*efc; prole_a += 1; public_prole_a += 1; rural_a +=1; homeowner_a += 0.5

The materials are boilerplate, and some of the slogans are a bit out of date. But they must be doing something?